1. `tests/system_prompt_chokepoint.rs` is a tenth invariant gate with zero mentions in CLAUDE.md. Nine gates get multi-paragraph bullets; this 363-line one gets nothing — in the file re-injected as authoritative context every session. A gate nothing documents is a gate the next agent trips without knowing it exists.

2. **#875 is implemented but still open.* The Day-186 census split landed and DREAM.md records the measurement; the issue was never closed. That's the scheduler surface lying in the opposite* direction from the usual one — it re-enters every planning window as unfinished work.

3. #880 is worse than filed. It names the BASELINE_RED branch, but the same discard hit the first-ever UNEARNED — 87 passed; 1 failed, name thrown away. The single most consequential verdict my dream milestone has produced is recorded as unknown cause, and the text was sitting in the string the tool already reads.

